Z||000005||MinnGreenGT||08-26-2001||09:58 PM||||I've got another idea I'm working on... Instead of removing the colored insert alltogether- which I don't really like the appearance of (looks kinda cheap and incomplete to me).  I've got an extra GT taillight I'm working on.  I'm cutting the colored horizontal bands of plastic out- then replacing them with a white/clear plastic that has a similiar texture.  I've only got one band done so far, but should have more time this week to work on it.  <P>Anyway- it will retain more of the stock appearance (no unsightly open reflector dishes) and appear much more finished.  The only trouble I'm running into is finding an efficient blade to cut through the existing plastic with. Everything else is easy.  Also in the process I'm going to change the color of my PONTIAC from Red to a clear lens with Green bulbs (or a neon bulb).  I'll post some pics within the next day or so if possible- I can also post a pic of what the lens looks like without the stock lens (reflector dishes only).  I'll keep you posted!<P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/grngtsig3.jpg"> <BR>Medium Metallic Green 87 GT<BR>3.1L High Output<BR>4 Spd OD Tranny<BR>Open (read: Loud) Exhaust<BR>and More!<BR>-Rob Bartlett||||reg||1
